From d6a57c141c8c6b4e7c382d2dbdad97f036141c3a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Substring <frog2wah@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 00:33:31 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/7] Add Wayland backend

Set modes through the compositor with wlr-output-management. Version 5
of the protocol carries full timings; with older versions only modes
advertised by the compositor are used, since it would otherwise pick
its own timings for the requested size.

The backend is preferred when WAYLAND_DISPLAY is set, as Xwayland only
emulates XRANDR modes.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
