From 0f202e0c97cbfe17650eded2167b7374d12aff8c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Substring <frog2wah@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 18:20:59 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 3/7] Wayland: support KWin through kde-output-management

KWin doesn't implement wlr-output-management, but version 22 of
kde-output-management-v2 carries full timings: register the modeline
as a custom mode (add_cvt, set_custom_modes), then select it.

The custom mode list replaces all custom modes, and KWin regenerates
all modes of the output on each list: the user's custom modes are kept,
and our unused modes are dropped along with the new one rather than
after the mode switch.

Also track header dependencies of the Wayland backend in the makefile.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
