GroovyMAME passes the screen as "screen0", as the xrandr and drmkms
backends accept it. Positions, given as screenN or N, now count the
enabled outputs, so screen0 is the same output as auto.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 custom_video_wayland.cpp | 16 +++++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/custom_video_wayland.cpp b/custom_video_wayland.cpp
index 477a0c7..a6b5b67 100644
--- a/custom_video_wayland.cpp
+++ b/custom_video_wayland.cpp
@@ -636,13 +636,23 @@ bool wayland_timing::sync()
 
 wayland_head *wayland_timing::find_head()
 {
-	// Explicit output: connector name or index
+	// Explicit output: connector name, or position among the enabled outputs
+	// ("screen[0-9]" or a number, as with the other backends)
 	if (!m_head_name.empty())
 	{
+		const char *pos = m_head_name.c_str();
+		if (!strncmp(pos, "screen", 6) && pos[6] != 0)
+			pos += 6;
+
 		char *end;
-		long index = strtol(m_head_name.c_str(), &end, 10);
+		long index = strtol(pos, &end, 10);
 		if (*end == 0)
-			return (index >= 0 && index < (long)m_heads.size()) ? m_heads[index] : nullptr;
+		{
+			for (auto head : m_heads)
+				if (head->enabled && index-- == 0)
+					return head;
+			return nullptr;
+		}
 
 		for (auto head : m_heads)
 			if (head->name == m_head_name)

From 0ff7e7472f591e6c768b09c068d1009bda422a54 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Substring <frog2wah@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 13:32:18 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 7/7] DRM/KMS: lease the connector from the Wayland compositor

Under a Wayland compositor, which is the DRM master of the device,
opening the device gives no modesetting rights. When WAYLAND_DISPLAY is
set, the DRM/KMS backend now leases the connector through
wp-drm-lease-v1 (labwc leases any output, the one of its desktop
included) and applies itself to the lease fd: it is master over the
leased connector, its CRTC and its plane. The compositor takes the
connector back when the backend is destroyed.

The compositor disables a connector it leases, which then has no
encoder: the leased CRTC is used, with its index on the whole device,
which vblank requests refer to.

The lease is built when both the DRM/KMS and the Wayland support are.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
